"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, launched in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the project leader. The project has received a $2M budget approval from the executive board. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, leading to the development phase led by Omar Jensen, and the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Recent progress includes a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated effective January next year. Additionally, a $15,000 budget has been approved for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, starting next month. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November. The project also involves collaboration with Zenith Innovations, with onboarding scheduled for April 15th, 2023."
